| `UNDEFINED-TOKEN` | a `.css` file under `ui/`/`ui_admin/` touched | every `var(--app-x)` referenced resolves: `--app-x:` is declared in some file under `app/` (stylesheets, templates, served pages, Python that emits CSS) or set by script (`setProperty`/`style[]`) — a name defined nowhere is a dead token and the var() silently resolves to its fallback or nothing (the invisible-pressed-state class, 13-design-spec.mdc banned basins). One failure lists every file+name — a systemic class is one finding | `EXEMPT-TOKEN: <file or *> — <where it is defined>` |
